From 8854e5a821a54c402267cb8b96867a6e5b26d88a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saravanakumar A <asaravanakumar2k3@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:57:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: flash: flash_renesas_ra_ospi_b: reset the configured
 chip-select

flash_renesas_ra_ospi_b_spi_mode_init() resets the attached flash by
driving the OM_RESET line for chip-select 0 only:

	R_XSPI0->LIOCTL_b.RSTCS0 = 0;
	k_sleep(K_USEC(500));
	R_XSPI0->LIOCTL_b.RSTCS0 = 1;

But the device may be attached to chip-select 1 (the driver configures
.channel = OSPI_B_DEVICE_NUMBER_1), and RSTCS0/RSTCS1 are independent
bits in XSPI0.LIOCTL. RSTCS1 is never written anywhere in the driver, so
on a board whose OSPI-B flash is on CS1 (e.g. ek_ra8d1, whose s28hl512t
node is at reg = <0x90000000 ...>) the "reset flash device" step does
nothing and the device can be left in a non-1S protocol mode across a
warm reboot.

The same function two lines earlier already indexes the CS correctly
(R_XSPI0->LIOCFGCS_b[p_ctrl->channel].DDRSMPEX). Make the reset match by
selecting RSTCS0/RSTCS1 from p_ctrl->channel.

Found by code inspection during ek_ra8d1 bring-up; not functionally
verified because the OSPI NOR on the board sample in hand is
non-responsive (unrelated hardware issue).

Signed-off-by: Saravanakumar A <asaravanakumar2k3@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/flash/flash_renesas_ra_ospi_b.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/flash/flash_renesas_ra_ospi_b.c b/drivers/flash/flash_renesas_ra_ospi_b.c
index 7dbb77696d5..62733f53ae2 100644
--- a/drivers/flash/flash_renesas_ra_ospi_b.c
+++ b/drivers/flash/flash_renesas_ra_ospi_b.c
@@ -171,10 +171,22 @@ static int flash_renesas_ra_ospi_b_spi_mode_init(ospi_b_instance_ctrl_t *p_ctrl,
 		return -EIO;
 	}
 
-	/* Reset flash device by driving OM_RESET pin */
-	R_XSPI0->LIOCTL_b.RSTCS0 = 0;
-	k_sleep(K_USEC(500));
-	R_XSPI0->LIOCTL_b.RSTCS0 = 1;
+	/* Reset flash device by driving the OM_RESET pin of the *configured*
+	 * chip-select. The attached device may be on CS0 or CS1
+	 * (p_ctrl->channel, as used just above for LIOCFGCS). Unconditionally
+	 * driving RSTCS0 never resets a device wired to CS1 (e.g. the S28HL512T
+	 * on the EK-RA8D1, reg = <0x90000000 ...>), so it can be left in a
+	 * non-1S protocol mode across a warm reboot.
+	 */
+	if (p_ctrl->channel == OSPI_B_DEVICE_NUMBER_1) {
+		R_XSPI0->LIOCTL_b.RSTCS1 = 0;
+		k_sleep(K_USEC(500));
+		R_XSPI0->LIOCTL_b.RSTCS1 = 1;
+	} else {
+		R_XSPI0->LIOCTL_b.RSTCS0 = 0;
+		k_sleep(K_USEC(500));
+		R_XSPI0->LIOCTL_b.RSTCS0 = 1;
+	}
 	k_sleep(K_NSEC(50));
 
 	/* Transfer write enable command */
-- 
